<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">António Vicente da Cruz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">António Vicente da Cruz, known as Bonga, was a member of the Afro-Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/da-cruz-family">Da Cruz family</a> who ruled Massangano on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a> in the mid-nineteenth century. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chikunda">Chikunda</a> soldiers based in stockaded forts, he controlled river traffic and destroyed several Portuguese expeditions sent against him between 1867 and 1869, making his state a leading independent power on the lower Zambezi.</p></div>
